  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tanzania Vector Control Activity</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Tanzania):  With FY 2022 funds, USAID will continue maintaining high levels of access to and use of long-lasting insecticide-treated nets (ITNs) across the 26 regions of Tanzania with the highest burden of malaria. This will be accomplished through continuous or annual delivery of ITNs through public primary schools, targeted mass replacement campaigns, and, in Zanzibar, through health facilities and mass replacement campaign channels. The activity will provide technical guidance to the Government of Tanzania (GOT) on innovative and evidence-based vector control approaches. As appropriate, and in line with the President&apos;s Malaria Initiative (PMI) Headquarters technical guidance, the activity may also assist with the implementation and piloting of new vector control approaches.  .</narrative>
  </description>
